  None,
  'Ukrainska Pravda, citing Kharkiv regional governor Oleh Syniehubov, reports that on the night of 21 October Russian drones attacked the village of Korotych in Kharkiv district: an 81-year-old woman and an 83-year-old man were killed, another 11 people, among them a 2-month-old boy and an 8-year-old girl, suffered acute stress reactions, and 13 private houses were damaged. In Kremenchuk a drone hit an academic building of Kremenchuk National University: according to the emergency service, two people were injured and a 16-year-old girl was hospitalised, while the Poltava regional governor speaks of two injured. Rector Denys Zahirniak told Suspilne that no one was hurt in the Geran strike, only the doorkeeper was badly frightened.',
